and governors across the Almoravid empire.’  ‘The Almoravid ruling elite was thus an amalgam of Sanhaja ad non-Sanhaja constituencies bound together by their mutual adherence to the Maliki school of law and military supported not only by the veiled desert tribes, but also by Maghribi, Andalusi and Christian contingents who perceived their interests to lie with the regime.’ '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1651, 'temperature': 0.2})
