volving, shaped, it seems, by the complexities of alliance building and favour seeking. That the priestly elite maintained some autonomy and influence was best illustrated during royal succession struggles, when shrine heads sometimes accepted the risks involved in partisanship." '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 2434, 'temperature': 0.2})
