stice, and each deity was acknowledged as having its own specific laws, the Aro-Chukwu oracle was a respected source of guidance and religious inspiration. One finds, then a connection between Igbo religion (Aro-Chukwu) and Igbo morality in the use of an oracle to make decisions and also the development of economic forms of social exchange.” '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 2687, 'temperature': 0.2})
