 brought elite Wutai monks into direct contact with powerful Tibetan lamas. For instance, Monk Xiong (Xiong jixiang 雄吉祥), after serving in one such assembly at Dadu in 1276, was promoted by the National Preceptor—Rin himself—to the post of Chief Buddhist Judge (dusengpan 都僧判) on Mt. Wutai. Similar privileges awaited other Chinese monks subsequently accorded elite titles and positions on Mt. Wutai.”  '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 2827, 'temperature': 0.2})
