itarian’ (Freeman 1955b: 10). This conclusion has since been confirmed by other systematically trained ethnographers who have studied Iban society at depth.” (Freeman, 1891, 1)  “This way of life, the religious focus on the rice cult, an economy based almost exclusively on hill rice cultivation and social organization centred on the longhouse community of separate bilek families – this way of life, which has survived for centuries, if not already close to extinction, is likely to disappear with the older generation of living Iban.” '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1467, 'temperature': 0.2})
